From 81c5c06f8684ea74fe3990052da3598082faec27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dean Harmon <deannetharmon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:55:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Classify standalone long-dated calls as LEAPS instead of
 UNKNOWN

Adds a LEAPS branch to classifyPositionLifecycle() (lib/portfolio/positionLifecycle.ts):
a long call with no paired short call, no puts, and DTE > 120 (reusing PMCC's existing
long-leg threshold for consistency) now classifies as LEAPS instead of falling through to
UNKNOWN. Scoped to calls only -- a standalone long put is not treated as a LEAP in this app's
context, since LEAPS here specifically anchors a future covered-call/PMCC foundation.

Ordered after the PMCC check so a long call that already has a qualifying short call sold
against it still classifies as PMCC, not LEAPS.

lib/portfolio-data/acquisition.ts: narrows the new, broader PositionLifecycleType down to
RemainingOpportunityLifecycle at the two call sites feeding scorePortfolioRemainingOpportunity/
calculateRemainingOpportunity. LEAPS positions are debit-based (bought, not sold for credit)
and don't semantically belong in %-of-credit-captured scoring, so LEAPS maps to UNKNOWN there
rather than widening that type to accept a value it has no real meaning for.

9 new tests covering the LEAPS branch (standalone call, short-dated exclusion, DTE boundary,
PMCC precedence, put exclusion, mixed-DTE group rejection, unparseable-symbol safety).

Verified: 19/19 positionLifecycle tests pass, full regression suite shows zero new failures
(3 pre-existing failures in greekAcquisitionWiring.test.ts confirmed present on clean main
before this change), typecheck shows the same 41 pre-existing errors as clean main baseline,
zero new.
